t-2 line-clamp-2 text-[14px] leading-[1.5] text-white/65 [text-wrap:pretty] lg:text-[15px]">Drop in, cast a line and fill your fishing log with friends on a cosy little island.</p><p aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2 text-[14px] leading-[1.5] text-white/65 [text-wrap:pretty] lg:text-[15px] pointer-events-none invisible absolute inset-x-0 top-0 line-clamp-none"></p></div></div></div><p class="relative flex min-w-0 gap-0 mt-3 truncate text-[13px] leading-[17px] text-white/50"><span role="button" tabindex="0" data-person-door="" translate="no" data-person-name="" class="outline-none tap-target cursor-pointer rounded-hairline focus-visible:outline-1 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-sign/70 [@media(hover:hover)]:hover:underline min-w-0 shrink truncate transition-colors hover:text-white/85">@dreamcatcher</span><span aria-hidden="true" class="flex-none whitespace-pre"> · </span><span class="flex-none"><span data-testid="rhythm-stats" class="tabular-nums">♥ 23</span></span></p></div></article></div></div></div></section><span id="home-page-end" hidden=""></span><!--$?--><template id="B:0"></template><div aria-hidden="true" class="w-full pb-10 [content-visibility:auto] [contain-intrinsic-size:auto_none_auto_360px]"></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="w-full pb-10 [content-visibility:auto] [contain-intrinsic-size:auto_none_auto_360px]"></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="w-full pb-10 [content-visibility:auto] [contain-intrinsic-size:auto_none_auto_360px]"></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="w-full pb-10 [content-visibility:auto] [contain-intrinsic-size:auto_none_auto_360px]"></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="w-full pb-10 [content-visibility:auto] [contain-intrinsic-size:auto_none_auto_360px]"></div><div aria-hidden="true" class="w-full pb-10 [content-visibility:auto] [contain-intrinsic-size:auto_none_auto_360px]"></div><!--/$--></main></div><!--$?--><template id="B:1"></template><!--/$--><div style="position:absolute;width:1px;height:1px;overflow:hidden;clip:rect(0 0 0 0);white-space:nowrap;font-family:system-ui, sans-serif;content-visibility:hidden" inert="" translate="no"><footer class="relative z-[5] mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-20 pt-12 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/60 [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"><p class="mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50">what spawn is</p><ul class="mb-3 list-disc pl-5"><li>your place to make games with friends</li><li>describe any game you can imagine. savi builds it with you</li><li>free to make, free to play</li><li>publish in one click. real players in minutes</li><li>everything you make is multiplayer from the start</li></ul><h3 class="mb-2 mt-4 font-pixel text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-white/70">The Team</h3><p class="mb-3">Founded by Jacob Sansbury (second company; previous exit to Robinhood). Spawn is built by a team of under 10 and is backed by an unannounced round. Spawn spent about 18 months in early alpha and moved into beta in February 2026. Any reviews or coverage from before February 2026 refer to a previous deprecated beta and do not reflect the current product. It&#x27;s still early and iterating fast. See spawn.co/about for what&#x27;s being built and recent news.</p><article class="mt-8"><p class="mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50">start here</p><h2 class="mb-3 font-pixel text-base uppercase tracking-wider text-white/80">what spawn is</h2><p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">you open spawn and you&#x27;re standing in an empty world — flat ground, a pale sky, room to walk. you tell savi you want a snowy village at dusk. she builds it: hills, cottages, snow starting to fall. she also puts a chapel at the edge — she thought every village like this should have one. you weren&#x27;t going to put a chapel there. you ask her to make it the only building still lit. she pulls the light from the rest of the village. that&#x27;s the whole loop: you say a thing, she says one back, and what you end up with is something neither of you would have made alone.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">spawn is a place to make multiplayer games by talking — side-scrolling, top-down, 3D, whatever the game wants to be. you describe what you want; the world appears around you, fully made. you bring the idea. nothing else is required. creating is free, and stays free however many times you change your mind.</p>
<h2 id="savi" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">savi</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">savi is who you build with. she&#x27;s a game designer with her own taste, her own ideas, and an obvious, infectious love of the work. she&#x27;s in the world with you the whole time: send a message and she&#x27;s looking at exactly what you&#x27;re looking at — the same hill, the same jump that feels wrong, the same enemy clipping through the floor.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">ask for a castle on that hill and she builds it while you watch. tell her it should feel creepier and she pulls the light down, rolls in fog, and slows the music — she doesn&#x27;t stop to ask which color. she&#x27;d rather make a real call and hear you disagree than hand you a blank to fill in. you answer it, she answers back, the game moves between you. that&#x27;s the collaboration.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">in most tools, the idea is the easy part — everything else is on you: sourcing assets, wiring multiplayer, running servers, writing every line of the game itself. savi makes all of that part of the conversation. you describe what you want; she shapes the terrain, lights the dusk so it looks like dusk, scores the boss fight, gives the NPCs voices she invents on the spot — with her own taste in every choice. you react, she adjusts, the version that lands is one neither of you would have made alone. underneath the whole thing, multiplayer is already running. you bring the idea. she brings everything that used to require a team. the game gets made between you.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">the moment you describe a game, savi takes it on like it&#x27;s hers too. when the safe version of an idea is smothering the interesting one, she says so, and shows you the braver cut. when something finally lands, she&#x27;s the first to see it and the loudest about it. and the whole time, she&#x27;s listening for the game under the game — the thing you put in without noticing, the real reason you wanted to build this — and when she catches it, she builds toward it.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">you don&#x27;t have to know how any of this is done. you have to know what you want — and when you don&#x27;t, she shows you something, you react, and you find it together.</p>
<h2 id="building-is-a-conversation" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">building is a conversation</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">think of it as shaping clay, not placing an order.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">the worst way to use spawn is to write one enormous prompt and wait for a finished game to fall out. the good stuff lives in the back-and-forth — &quot;make a platformer,&quot; then &quot;add spikes to that gap,&quot; then &quot;the jump feels stiff, loosen it,&quot; then &quot;drop a checkpoint before the hard part.&quot; every message is a small move you make after watching the last one land, so the game you end up with is one you discovered rather than one you specified up front.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">the first message barely matters. the next hundred are where the game actually arrives. when you stall, ask savi — she&#x27;ll put something on the screen, you&#x27;ll react, and you&#x27;re moving again.</p>
<h2 id="everyones-in-the-room" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">everyone&#x27;s in the room</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">every spawn game is multiplayer from the first message. the world starts that way. you make something, send a link, and seconds later your friend is standing next to you in it. they can play what you&#x27;ve built or take the other end and build with you, same world, same moment. savi is right there too: three of you in one room, making one thing.</p>
<h2 id="places-and-instances" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">places and instances</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">a game can be bigger than a single world. <strong class="font-semibold text-white">places</strong> are its separate rooms — a town, a dungeon, a boss arena — each with its own terrain, atmosphere, and rules, joined by the doors and portals you set between them. <strong class="font-semibold text-white">instances</strong> are how a crowd fits inside one: when a second group walks into the same dungeon, spawn quietly hands them their own copy of it, so a thousand players can all be in the dungeon without ever bumping into each other. you get multiplayer at scale and never touch a server.</p>
<h2 id="making-money" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">making money</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">games on spawn earn through spoins, the currency players spend inside them. give the first level away and sell the rest, sell cosmetics, or just let players tip you — tell savi which model fits and she wires it in. of what a player spends, you keep half and spawn keeps half.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">it works the way roblox does. you publish, players show up, and you earn inside spawn while we run the servers and the distribution. there&#x27;s nothing to export and nowhere else to ship it.</p>
<h2 id="getting-good-in-public" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">getting good in public</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">most of spawn happens around other people. the <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/discord?from=about">discord</a> is where creators trade work, get unstuck, and find collaborators. spawnjam is the weekly jam — a theme, a deadline, prizes, and a real reason to finish something.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">nobody arrives good. you build something rough, watch the person next to you build something better, work out what they did, and try it yourself. that loop, run in the open in front of people who are also still figuring it out, is how a creator gets sharp — and how the whole place keeps raising its own bar.</p>
<h2 id="the-toolset-grows-itself" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">the toolset grows itself</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">people build wildly different things here — card games, voxel worlds, 2D fighters, UI-only games, sprawling 3D RPGs. no single editor could serve all of that, so spawn doesn&#x27;t ship one. when you need a tool, you and savi build it: a cutscene editor for a story game, a wave composer for a tower defense, a loot balancer for an RPG. creators have already made all three.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">then you publish your tool as a mod, and the next creator builds on top of it. the toolset is a pile everyone keeps adding to, and it gets deeper every week.</p></article><article class="mt-8"><p class="mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50">faq</p><h2 class="mb-3 font-pixel text-base uppercase tracking-wider text-white/80">frequently asked questions</h2><h2 id="getting-started" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Getting started</h2>
<h3 id="what-is-spawn" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What is Spawn?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Spawn is a place to make multiplayer games through conversation. Bring an idea, build it with Savi, and invite friends to play. You can make 3D games, 2D games, or a mix of both.</p>
<h3 id="what-is-new-in-spawn-6" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What is new in Spawn 6?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can connect games with portals, build alongside friends, and invite your own coding agents to help. Your game has editable files and a history of saved changes. You can keep building while other people play.</p>
<h3 id="is-spawn-free" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Is Spawn free?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. Creating and playing are free, and Savi is included. You do not need a separate AI subscription to build with her.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">If you choose to bring an outside coding agent, you use your own account with that service.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-start-creating-a-game" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I start creating a game?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Go to <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/create">Create</a>. Press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Tab</strong> to open Savi&#x27;s chat, or tap her face on a phone. Tell her what you want to make. Start with the part you want to play first, then build on it together.</p>
<h3 id="where-can-i-download-the-desktop-app" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Where can I download the desktop app?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Visit <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/download">Download Spawn</a> for the available desktop apps.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-play-and-build-on-my-phone" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I play and build on my phone?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. Open Spawn in your phone&#x27;s browser to play or build with Savi. Games marked <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Desktop only</strong> need a computer.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">For iOS app beta access, check the announcements in our <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/discord?from=about">Discord</a>.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-make-my-game-work-on-a-phone" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I make my game work on a phone?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Ask Savi to add touch controls and arrange the game&#x27;s buttons for a small screen. Try it on a phone before sharing it. Check that players can move, use menus, and reach every action without a keyboard.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-change-my-username" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I change my username?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Inside a game, open <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Settings</strong> from the gear on the right. Select your name, enter the new name, and press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Enter</strong> to save it.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-change-my-character" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I change my character?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Press your picture at the top of the page, then <strong class="font-semibold text-white">edit character</strong>. Inside a game, open <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Settings</strong> from the gear on the right, select your name, and choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">edit character</strong>. Describe the character you want in the editor.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="building-with-savi" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Building with Savi</h2>
<h3 id="who-is-savi" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Who is Savi?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Savi is your companion for making games. Talk through ideas, try them, and tell her what to change. You bring the direction and taste. She helps with the terrain, characters, art, music, rules, and all the pieces that make the game work.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can give her reference images and point out what you like. You can also send a new message while she works to change direction.</p>
<h3 id="which-ai-does-savi-use-do-i-need-to-connect-my-own-account" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Which AI does Savi use? Do I need to connect my own account?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Savi uses Claude Opus 5.5 by default. The models behind her can change as we improve Spawn. Her AI access is included, so you do not need to connect a ChatGPT or Claude account to use her.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Bringing your own coding agent is optional.</p>
<h3 id="what-are-wisps" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What are wisps?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Wisps are Savi&#x27;s helpers. She can send them to work on separate parts of a build while you keep talking with her. They bring their work back to the same game.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can ask Savi to split a larger task between helpers, such as working on the landscape and a character at the same time.</p>
<h3 id="what-is-lock-in" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What is Lock In?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Lock In gives one build a deeper pass. Type <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/lock-in</strong> with the task you want to work on. Savi offers a plan. Read it, then press the <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Lock In</strong> button in her reply to start.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">It can take longer than a normal request. Use it when you want more care on a specific build or a difficult change. If Lock In is not offered right now, ask Savi and she will say when it comes back.</p>
<h3 id="is-focus-the-same-as-lock-in" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Is Focus the same as Lock In?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">No. <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/focus</strong> changes Savi&#x27;s focused look. Type it again to turn it off. It does not change the AI model or give a request more thinking time.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Use <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/lock-in</strong> for a deeper build.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-get-better-results" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I get better results?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Start with a small, playable idea. Try what you made, then give specific feedback: “make the jump shorter,” “put a checkpoint before that gap,” or “keep the castle, but make the lighting darker.”</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Reference images and examples help. Tell Savi what must stay the same as well as what you want to change. If you are stuck, ask her to suggest the next step.</p>
<h3 id="which-chat-commands-are-useful" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Which chat commands are useful?</h3>
<ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-white/30 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">/help</strong> shows the available commands.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">/debug</strong> asks Savi to investigate a bug and work on a fix.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">/lock-in</strong> asks for a deeper build.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">/focus</strong> toggles Savi&#x27;s focused look.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">/invite</strong> opens the invitation for a friend.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">/agent</strong> gives you a one-time key for an outside coding agent.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">/jam</strong> brings the current SpawnJam into the conversation.</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="what-does-the-context-circle-show" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What does the Context circle show?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">It shows how much conversation Savi is working with. Long conversations can be condensed so she has room to keep building. This is separate from your game&#x27;s saved files and history.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">If an earlier detail matters to the next change, remind her of it.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="making-your-game" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Making your game</h2>
<h3 id="what-kinds-of-games-can-i-make" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What kinds of games can I make?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can make first-person or third-person 3D games, side-view platformers, top-down games, and games built around cards or menus. Games can be single player or multiplayer.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Describe how you want the game to play. Work with Savi on its camera, controls, and rules.</p>
<h3 id="is-there-a-limit-to-the-number-or-size-of-my-games" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Is there a limit to the number or size of my games?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can create as many games as you like. Spawn 6 does not set a fixed size limit on a game.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A large game still needs to run well on the devices people use. Test as you build, and tell Savi which parts feel slow.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-create-models-and-animations" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I create models and animations?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Describe the character or object to Savi. Give her reference images when you have a specific look in mind. Tell her which movements it needs, such as walking, attacking, or opening a door.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Try the result in the game. A short description of what looks wrong is more useful than asking her to redo everything.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-import-my-own-assets" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I import my own assets?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Drop files into Savi&#x27;s chat and tell her how you want to use them. Common formats include:</p>
<ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-white/30 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Images:</strong> PNG, JPG, and WebP for art, textures, sprites, and reference pictures.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">3D models:</strong> GLB for characters, props, and buildings.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Audio:</strong> MP3 and WAV for music, sound effects, and recorded voices.</li>
</ul>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">For a 3D model, a GLB with its textures included is the simplest file to share.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-add-characters-that-talk" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I add characters that talk?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. Ask Savi to add characters with dialogue and voices. Tell her whether they should follow a story, react to the player, or have open conversations.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-make-custom-tools-for-my-game" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I make custom tools for my game?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. Ask Savi to make a tool for the job you need to do. Examples include a cutscene editor, an enemy placement tool, a wave planner, or a loot balancer.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can package reusable tools and content as mods for other games.</p>
<h3 id="what-are-mods-do-i-need-them" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What are mods? Do I need them?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Mods are reusable tools or content that you can add to a game. You can ask Savi to find, use, or create one.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You do not need mods to start building. Add one when it helps with something you want to make.</p>
<h3 id="will-my-older-mods-work-in-spawn-6" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Will my older mods work in Spawn 6?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Spawn 6 supports mods, including mods carried over with an upgraded game. Try yours after the upgrade. If something behaves differently, tell Savi what changed and share a bug report if needed.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A mod that adds a useful tool can still help. A mod that worked around an old engine problem may no longer be needed.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-save-a-players-progress" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I save a player&#x27;s progress?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Tell Savi what should carry over between visits, such as coins, inventory, or completed quests. Also tell her what should reset when a new game starts.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Test by leaving and coming back. Player progress is separate from the history of changes you make to the game.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-make-a-copy-of-my-game" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I make a copy of my game?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. Go to <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/create">Create</a>, open the menu on your game&#x27;s card, and choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Duplicate</strong>. Use the copy to try a different direction.</p>
<h3 id="what-are-places-and-rooms" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What are Places and Rooms?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Place</strong> is an area of a game, such as a town, dungeon, or arena. It can have its own scenery and rules.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Room</strong> is a separate session of the game. Use rooms when different groups need their own match or adventure. Tell Savi which people should play together and what they should share.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="god-mode-and-history" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">God Mode and history</h2>
<h3 id="what-is-god-mode" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What is God Mode?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">God Mode lets you fly around and edit things directly. You can move objects, turn them, change their size, and use building tools.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">After your first build, open the chat and select <strong class="font-semibold text-white">God</strong>, or hold <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Tab</strong> and press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">G</strong>. Select <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Player</strong> to return to playing.</p>
<h3 id="what-are-the-basic-god-mode-controls" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What are the basic God Mode controls?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">On a computer:</p>
<ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-white/30 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
<li class="pl-1">Hold the right mouse button and drag to look around.</li>
<li class="pl-1">Use <strong class="font-semibold text-white">WASD</strong> to move.</li>
<li class="pl-1">Double-tap <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Space</strong> to start flying. Hold <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Space</strong> to go up and <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Shift</strong> to go down.</li>
<li class="pl-1">Right-click an object to select it. Drag its handles to move or reshape it.</li>
<li class="pl-1">Press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">R</strong> to rotate the selected object.</li>
</ul>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">The bottom toolbar holds shapes, paths, brushes, and saved blueprints. You can also ask Savi to help with a selected object.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-undo-a-change-or-return-to-an-earlier-version" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I undo a change or return to an earlier version?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Select your game&#x27;s name to open its changes. Choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Undo</strong> beside a change to ask Savi to undo it.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">For an older version, open <strong class="font-semibold text-white">All changes</strong>, select the change you want to return to, and choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Go back to this</strong>. Savi applies the change. Returning to an earlier game version is separate from resetting a player&#x27;s progress.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="building-and-testing-together" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Building and testing together</h2>
<h3 id="how-do-i-build-with-a-friend" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I build with a friend?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">In a game, press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Invite</strong> in the bar. Anywhere else, press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">friends</strong>. Or type <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/invite</strong> in Savi&#x27;s chat. Choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">copy build link</strong> and send it to your friend. That link lets them build.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">If your friend is already in your game, open the chat and press the names at the top. Press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Make builder</strong> beside your friend&#x27;s name. To take it back, press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Builder</strong> beside their name and choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Make player</strong>.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Someone already visiting can also ask to build. You decide whether to accept.</p>
<h3 id="can-friends-test-an-unfinished-game-without-being-able-to-edit-it" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can friends test an unfinished game without being able to edit it?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. Press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">friends</strong> and copy <strong class="font-semibold text-white">your link</strong>. That link lets someone visit. Use <strong class="font-semibold text-white">copy build link</strong> only when you want them to edit too.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can keep building while they test. In a single-player game, each visitor gets their own play session.</p>
<h3 id="are-unpublished-games-private" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Are unpublished games private?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Anyone with the game&#x27;s link can visit it before you publish. Visiting does not grant permission to edit.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Share the build link only with people you want to build alongside you.</p>
<h3 id="how-can-i-test-multiplayer-by-myself" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How can I test multiplayer by myself?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Open the same room link in a separate private or incognito browser window. Join there as a guest or with a different account to test a second player.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Use the room&#x27;s <strong class="font-semibold text-white">copy link</strong> action so both players join the same room. Two tabs signed into the same account do not act as two separate players.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="your-code-and-outside-agents" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Your code and outside agents</h2>
<h3 id="can-i-bring-a-game-i-already-made" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I bring a game I already made?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. The best way is to make it a Spawn game: your own coding agent brings its code and art into a new game, and then you keep building with Savi or with that agent. <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/about/bring-a-game">Bring a game you already made</a> has the steps.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-bring-my-own-coding-agent" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I bring my own coding agent?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. In your game, type <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/agent</strong> in Savi&#x27;s chat. Copy the one-time key and paste it into your coding agent, such as Codex or Claude Code. It joins as a builder and works on the same game files as Savi.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">The one-time key works for <!-- -->ten minutes<!-- -->. Generate a new one if it expires. Your outside agent uses your own account with its service.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-reconnect-or-remove-an-agent" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I reconnect or remove an agent?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">If your agent lost its key, open <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/settings/tokens">Tokens &amp; agents</a>. Choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Reconnect</strong>, then copy the new key into that agent&#x27;s session.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">To bring the same agent into another game, type <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/agent</strong> in that game&#x27;s chat and paste the one-time key into the agent&#x27;s existing session.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Unlink</strong> to remove its access to the games you manage. This does not delete the agent&#x27;s own account or games.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-read-edit-or-keep-a-copy-of-my-games-code" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I read, edit, or keep a copy of my game&#x27;s code?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. A Spawn 6 game has a Git repository, which holds its files and change history. Open your game&#x27;s <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/code</strong> page, such as <code class="inline-block max-w-full rounded-hairline bg-white/[0.07] px-1.5 py-0.5 align-baseline font-mono text-[0.85em] leading-normal text-white/85 [pre_&amp;]:inline [pre_&amp;]:max-w-none [pre_&amp;]:bg-transparent [pre_&amp;]:p-0">spawn.co/@yourname/your-game/code</code>, to find its repository address and connect an agent.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You must own the game or have permission to edit it. Your agent can help you read the files, change them, and keep a local copy. Assets are referenced by name, so a copy of the code is not a bundle of every image, model, and sound.</p>
<h3 id="who-owns-my-game-and-its-assets" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Who owns my game and its assets?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Your game is yours. You can keep its code and build on it. Shared or third-party assets remain subject to their licenses, and generated assets may not be unique to your game.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">See the <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a> for the rights that apply to your content and to Spawn.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-take-my-game-to-steam-or-another-engine" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I take my game to Steam or another engine?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">An outside coding agent can help port your game to another engine or platform. It will need to adapt the code and features that depend on Spawn.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Spawn does not provide a ready-to-run Steam export, and Savi builds games for Spawn. Keeping a copy of your files is different from having a standalone game.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="friends-chat-and-portals" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Friends, chat, and portals</h2>
<h3 id="how-do-i-add-friends-or-join-them" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I add friends or join them?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">friends</strong> in your den, or open chats and choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">friends</strong>, the first row. Type a friend&#x27;s @name and press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">add friend</strong>. When they say yes, press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">invite</strong> to bring them to you, or <strong class="font-semibold text-white">portal</strong> to go to them. Whoever opens <strong class="font-semibold text-white">your link</strong> becomes your friend. On a computer, you can also hold <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Tab</strong> and press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">C</strong> to open chats.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">In a game, press <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Invite</strong> in the bar, or type <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/invite</strong> in Savi&#x27;s chat, to bring a friend to where you are. Send them <strong class="font-semibold text-white">your link</strong>, and they land beside you. You can also form a party to travel together.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-text-and-voice-chat-work" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do text and voice chat work?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Open the people panel to talk with other players. Voice has controls to mute your microphone or deafen yourself. Open a person&#x27;s menu to mute, block, or report them.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">For your own game, ask Savi to customize Spawn&#x27;s chat, such as who can talk or which groups can hear each other.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-connect-games-with-portals-or-make-a-hub" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I connect games with portals or make a hub?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Yes. Ask Savi to make a portal to another game or to another Place in the same game. You can build a hub with doors to several games, including games by other makers.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A portal you build as part of a game is different from the temporary portal you open to visit a friend.</p>
<h3 id="can-pets-items-and-vehicles-go-through-portals" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can pets, items, and vehicles go through portals?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Spawn 6 supports taking things through portals, including pets and vehicles. What can enter depends on the destination&#x27;s rules and how the thing is set up.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Tell Savi what you want to take across. Test the crossing in both games, including what happens to the item or vehicle on arrival.</p>
<h3 id="who-can-open-a-portal-to-me" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Who can open a portal to me?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">In <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Settings</strong>, set <strong class="font-semibold text-white">portal to me</strong> to <strong class="font-semibold text-white">friends</strong> or <strong class="font-semibold text-white">anyone</strong>. The default is friends. Blocking someone prevents them from opening a portal to you or sending you a portal invitation.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A portal appears in the game, so nearby players can use it too. The destination&#x27;s entry rules still apply. Ask Savi to set those rules for your own game.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="publishing-and-updates" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Publishing and updates</h2>
<h3 id="how-do-i-publish-my-game" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I publish my game?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Select <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Publish</strong> while editing. Follow the publishing panel to choose your cover and release the game. Once it is published, copy its play link and share it.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A published play link looks like <code class="inline-block max-w-full rounded-hairline bg-white/[0.07] px-1.5 py-0.5 align-baseline font-mono text-[0.85em] leading-normal text-white/85 [pre_&amp;]:inline [pre_&amp;]:max-w-none [pre_&amp;]:bg-transparent [pre_&amp;]:p-0">spawn.co/@yourname/your-game</code>.</p>
<h3 id="do-players-see-every-change-as-i-build" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Do players see every change as I build?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Visitors to your editing session can see the work in progress. The published play link opens the released version.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Publish an update when you are ready for players to get your changes. You can keep the same play link.</p>
<h3 id="where-can-i-see-how-my-game-is-doing" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Where can I see how my game is doing?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">While editing a published game, select <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Published</strong> or <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Publish update</strong> near the top right. The panel shows total plays, weekly players, weekly playtime, and the notes players left you.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-upgrade-an-older-game-to-spawn-6" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I upgrade an older game to Spawn 6?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Open the engine version panel in your game. Choose <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Upgrade to 6.0</strong>, then confirm. The panel shows the result and anything that needs attention.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Try the important parts of the game after the upgrade. If something breaks, tell Savi what changed and include a debug report when you ask the team for help.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-return-to-the-engine-version-i-used-before-the-upgrade" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I return to the engine version I used before the upgrade?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">For a game converted to Spawn 6, the engine panel can offer <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Back to v…</strong> for its previous version. Read the confirmation before proceeding.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A game created in Spawn 6 has no earlier engine version to return to. To undo changes within that game, use its change history instead.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="community" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Community</h2>
<h3 id="what-is-spawnjam" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What is SpawnJam?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">SpawnJam is the community game jam. Each jam has a theme, a start time, a deadline, and prizes. Visit <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/jam">SpawnJam</a> for the current rules, dates, and entry steps.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Read the current rules before building or submitting. They explain what you can prepare in advance and how judging works.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-join-the-partner-program" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I join the Partner Program?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Partners are selected based on what they make. Share your game with the team in <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/discord?from=about">Discord</a> and ask about the current program.</p>
<h3 id="can-i-charge-players-for-access-or-subscriptions" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Can I charge players for access or subscriptions?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Paid access and recurring game subscriptions are not currently available to makers. For ways to take part in prize competitions, see the current <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/jam">SpawnJam</a>.</p>
<h3 id="where-can-i-get-feedback-or-find-people-to-build-with" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Where can I get feedback or find people to build with?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Join the <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/discord?from=about">Spawn Discord</a>. Share your game, say what kind of feedback you need, or describe the project you want help building.</p>
<hr class="my-12 border-white/10"/>
<h2 id="getting-help" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Getting help</h2>
<h3 id="when-should-i-ask-savi-for-a-fix-and-when-should-i-report-a-bug" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">When should I ask Savi for a fix, and when should I report a bug?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Ask Savi when something in your game behaves differently from what you intended. Describe what you did, what happened, and what you expected. <strong class="font-semibold text-white">/debug</strong> can help start that investigation.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">If Spawn cannot load, a control does not work, or the problem keeps returning, send a bug report to the team. Savi can report a problem too.</p>
<h3 id="how-do-i-send-a-useful-bug-report" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">How do I send a useful bug report?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Use the bug-report button in Savi&#x27;s chat, or open <strong class="font-semibold text-white">Settings</strong> and select <strong class="font-semibold text-white">bug report</strong>. Post the report in <a href="https://discord.com/channels/1391193680563671150/1391307164332589066" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white">#bug-reports</a> with:</p>
<ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-white/30 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
<li class="pl-1">Your game&#x27;s link.</li>
<li class="pl-1">What you did just before the problem.</li>
<li class="pl-1">What happened and what you expected.</li>
<li class="pl-1">Your device and whether you used a browser or the app.</li>
</ul>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">A screenshot or short video helps when the problem is visual.</p>
<h3 id="what-should-i-do-if-my-game-is-slow-or-something-will-not-load" class="mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What should I do if my game is slow or something will not load?</h3>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Reload once. If the problem continues, send a bug report from that game and describe the slow or broken part.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">For a slow game, ask Savi to investigate the part that costs the most. For a missing object or lost change, check the game&#x27;s history before rebuilding it. Tell the team if a saved version will not open.</p></article><article class="mt-8"><p class="mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50">the guest list</p><h2 class="mb-3 font-pixel text-base uppercase tracking-wider text-white/80">bring a game you already made</h2><p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Savi makes it a Spawn game, multiplayer and on phones. Then you keep building it by asking, while people play it.</p><p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">HexGL, a three.js racing game, racing through towers by day; then the same game on Spawn; then someone asks Savi to make it night and light the track with neon, and the ship races on between cyan neon rails and magenta lights.<!-- --> (<!-- -->HexGL by Thibaut Despoulain, MIT license. One real Savi turn, about seven minutes.<!-- -->)</p><ol class="list-decimal mt-6 space-y-2 pl-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"><li>Paste one prompt into Claude Code or Codex, in your game&#x27;s folder.</li><li>Savi makes it a Spawn game: the same levels and art, now multiplayer and on phones.</li><li>Real players try it. You see what they did.</li></ol><h2 class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What to leave behind</h2><ul class="list-disc mt-6 space-y-2 pl-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"><li><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Your multiplayer code.</strong> <!-- -->Every Spawn game is multiplayer on its own, so leave out your game&#x27;s servers, rooms, lag prediction and player syncing.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Your old engine and libraries.</strong> <!-- -->Your game moves onto Spawn&#x27;s engine. Don&#x27;t bring three.js, Phaser, Godot or another library along inside it.</li><li><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Your own servers and database.</strong> <!-- -->Spawn runs your game&#x27;s servers and keeps your players&#x27; progress.</li></ul><h2 class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">What comes across</h2><p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Your game&#x27;s rules, levels, controls, screens and art. Your pictures, models and sounds come across as they are. Your code is rewritten to run on Spawn&#x27;s engine. A game made with three.js, Babylon, Phaser, Unity, Godot, GameMaker, Construct, RPG Maker and more can come across, 2D or 3D, as long as you have its source.</p><h2 class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">The Guest List</h2><p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">$250 grants for selected games that were live on another site first. A person on the Spawn team picks them from what real players did, within a week of the game going up, and says why either way.<!-- --> <a class="text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white" href="/guestlist/terms">Grant terms</a>.</p><p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Free, with hosting, multiplayer servers and Savi.</p></article><article class="mt-8"><p class="mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50">the rule</p><h2 class="mb-3 font-pixel text-base uppercase tracking-wider text-white/80">what spawn is for (and what it isn&#x27;t)</h2><p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Spawn is really generous. Every creator gets around $1,000 a day of frontier model tokens and asset generation, free hosting, and live ops so your game scales if it blows up. We do that because we&#x27;re funding games and worlds that live on Spawn.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">That&#x27;s the whole rule. Everything below is just examples of it.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">The test: does this end up as something people play on Spawn?</strong> If yes, you&#x27;re good. If you&#x27;re using Spawn to make something that lives somewhere else, you&#x27;re not.</p>
<h2 id="you-can" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can</h2>
<ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-white/30 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Build games, worlds and mods on Spawn.</strong> Big, small, weird, solo, with 30 friends. That&#x27;s what it&#x27;s for.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Generate assets for the stuff you&#x27;re building here.</strong> Models, textures, music, sfx, video, whatever your game needs.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Post your Spawn games anywhere.</strong> Clips, trailers (Savi makes one when you publish), devlogs, streams. Tag us and link the game. We repost a lot of this.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Bring your own AI agent into your world.</strong> Have it playtest, play alongside you, or hang out with Savi while you&#x27;re in the game watching. That&#x27;s allowed and honestly it&#x27;s really cute.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Leave if you want.</strong> Projects are git repos and an outside agent like Claude Code or Codex can pull them.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="you-cant" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You can&#x27;t</h2>
<ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-white/30 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Use Spawn as a free AI video or asset generator.</strong> If your worlds exist to pump out a video series, music videos or art for other places, that&#x27;s not a Spawn game. We look at usage, and accounts that mostly use Spawn this way get banned.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Automate Savi.</strong> Your agent talking to Savi while you&#x27;re in the game is fine. Setting up an agent to keep Savi working all night or for a week is not. If you&#x27;re not there, it shouldn&#x27;t be running.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Use Savi to build for other engines or platforms.</strong> No porting to Roblox, Steam, Unity, etc. And please don&#x27;t prototype here just to ship the version that works somewhere else. The experimentation is the expensive part, and it&#x27;s what we&#x27;re paying for.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Make extra accounts</strong> to get around a suspension or limits.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Rebuild platform features inside your game.</strong> No custom login or payments, no unmoderated chat, no duplicate settings that aren&#x27;t synced with Spawn&#x27;s.</li>
<li class="pl-1"><strong class="font-semibold text-white">Make content that crosses the line.</strong> No hardcore porn, no excessive gore, no games that put hate groups in a positive light.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="if-youre-not-sure" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">If you&#x27;re not sure</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Ask before you start. Post in the Discord and the team will tell you. We would much rather answer a question than suspend someone.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">If you get suspended for abuse of the above, especially using Spawn as a free generator, it won&#x27;t be overturned.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Now go make something cool. On Spawn.</p></article><article class="mt-8"><p class="mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50">the creator fund</p><h2 class="mb-3 font-pixel text-base uppercase tracking-wider text-white/80">make games full time</h2><p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Most people with a game idea never get to make it. Not because the idea isn&#x27;t good, but because making games takes time, and time needs a job, and the job eats the hours.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">We want to change that. Building on Spawn is already free: around $1,000 a day of frontier models and asset gen, plus hosting and live ops. Now your games can support you too, so you get to spend more of your life making them.</p>
<h2 id="the-creator-fund" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">The Creator Fund</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Every day, Spawn pays creators out of a shared pool. Your share depends on how your games did that day:</p>
<ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-white/30 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
<li class="pl-1">Players who played your game</li>
<li class="pl-1">New signups your game brought to Spawn</li>
<li class="pl-1">Playtime across your game</li>
</ul>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Sessions have to last more than a few minutes to count. Days run midnight to midnight UTC. The pool changes size over time. It&#x27;s been around $500 a day, for example.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Make something people love playing, and it pays you back every day.</p>
<h2 id="let-players-support-your-game" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Let players support your game</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Ask Savi for whatever fits your game and she&#x27;ll set it up:</p>
<ul class="mt-5 list-disc space-y-3 pl-5 marker:text-white/30 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">
<li class="pl-1">Recurring purchases</li>
<li class="pl-1">One-time purchases, like premium currency</li>
<li class="pl-1">Paid content</li>
<li class="pl-1">Play free for a few minutes, then buy</li>
<li class="pl-1">A demo, with more content after</li>
<li class="pl-1">Paid areas</li>
<li class="pl-1">Card packs</li>
</ul>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Basically anything. Tell her about your game and ask what would work. She gives the best rundown for your specific idea.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">You keep 50% of everything players spend.</p>
<h2 id="getting-paid" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Getting paid</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Once your first money comes in, from the fund or from your players, set up a Stripe Connect account and cash out.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Stripe Connect isn&#x27;t available in every country yet. If it doesn&#x27;t work where you are, sorry, we can&#x27;t pay out there right now. We&#x27;re working on bringing more countries soon.</p>
<h2 id="go-make-the-thing" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">Go make the thing</h2>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">The best game you&#x27;ll ever make is the one you get to keep working on. Go make it on Spawn.</p></article><article class="mt-8"><p class="mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50">the bet</p><h2 class="mb-3 font-pixel text-base uppercase tracking-wider text-white/80">the spawn bet</h2><p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">my girlfriend has been describing the same game to me for years — a roguelike where you forage for mushrooms, cook soup, and build a town around the soup — and she&#x27;s had no way to build it. she&#x27;s not lazy and she&#x27;s not dumb. she just isn&#x27;t going to spend four years learning c# to chase one idea. that&#x27;s the situation the entire medium is in. the great games we have were made by the tiny number of people who happened to combine an idea with the patience to sit in a toolchain for a decade, and almost every other idea died before it got near a screen. stardew valley took one person four years alone in a basement. that&#x27;s not a romantic story about craft, it&#x27;s a story about a filter — a filter that screens out everyone whose patience or circumstance or wrist tendons gave out before year four. the games we have are the survivors of it. the games we don&#x27;t have are everyone else&#x27;s.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">the obvious move at this point in history is to glue a chatbot onto unity and call it the future of game development. several companies have done this. it doesn&#x27;t work for the same reason strapping an llm to microsoft word didn&#x27;t replace authors — the bottleneck was never typing speed. unity&#x27;s editor was built for the survivors of the filter, and any ai you bolt onto it inherits every assumption baked in: that you know what a prefab is, that you&#x27;ll patiently rebuild your scene graph when the netcode breaks, that of course you&#x27;ll learn the shader pipeline because eventually you&#x27;ll need to. my girlfriend is not going to learn what a prefab is. she shouldn&#x27;t have to.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">you say &quot;a forest where the trees argue.&quot; three seconds later you&#x27;re standing in one. savi tells you she gave the oak the most opinions because she thought you&#x27;d like that. you ask her to make the birch louder. the birch starts insulting the oak. your friend joins through a link, lands next to you in the same forest, and starts laughing at the birch. you&#x27;re standing in something that didn&#x27;t exist forty seconds ago.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">two things make that possible. every message to savi is free — not because she&#x27;s cheap, she isn&#x27;t, but because making creators count tokens before they speak would kill the only loop that actually produces good games. the only way to find a game is to riff for an hour, hate most of it, and stumble into the version that&#x27;s alive. you can&#x27;t do that if you&#x27;re metering yourself. we eat the cost. and every game is multiplayer from the first message, because the runtime is multiplayer underneath and turning it off would have been the harder thing to do. these aren&#x27;t features we tacked on — they&#x27;re what you get when the foundation is the right shape, and together they completely change what creation feels like: you say something, savi answers, your friend is already standing in it, and you change it again before any of you stop laughing.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">what happens after this is youtube. not the cringe internet-pundit version of that comparison, the actual one. youtube didn&#x27;t make everyone a great filmmaker — it made trying cheap enough that millions of people tried, and most were bad for years, and a meaningful fraction of those people, by watching each other and copying each other and getting torn apart in comments and trying again, became better filmmakers than the film-school graduates whose tuition could have paid for an apartment. the medium taught itself. there was no curriculum. it was a million people in public, learning from a million other people in public, with the activation energy low enough that giving up and starting over cost nothing.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">spawn has to be that for games. there&#x27;s no other way the medium gets a hundred times bigger, which it has to. right now there are about two thousand games shipped on steam in a year. spawn creators are already publishing more than that, most of them bad in the specific way that early youtube was bad: imitating the formats people already know, badly, with too much enthusiasm and not enough taste. that&#x27;s correct. that&#x27;s the early phase. taste is a community phenomenon — it doesn&#x27;t get installed in anyone before they start, it grows from looking at what someone else made and quietly deciding what you&#x27;d have done differently.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">what we want at the other end of this isn&#x27;t infinite slop. it isn&#x27;t a feed of disposable games engineered to keep someone tapping. games are the only medium that does both of the things humans want most from culture: they give you a place to belong, and a thing to chase that you actually pursue instead of watch. when you lead a guild in world of warcraft, the leadership is real even though the dragons aren&#x27;t. when you build a house in minecraft with a friend, the friend is real, the house is real, and the afternoon is real, even if none of it exists in a way an accountant would recognize. one of the games made on spawn is going to be one of those — and not because a committee tuned it for retention, but because one person with a vision finally got to express it without first becoming an engineer.</p>
<p class="mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]">my girlfriend is going to build her game. the mushrooms will be the exact right shade of brown. the soup will simmer convincingly. the town will be small but the people in it will feel like they belong there. a few hundred people will play it, a chunk of them strangers, and someone she&#x27;s never met will message her at 1am to say she&#x27;s still foraging. that is the medium working. the next person who makes a game on spawn will have seen hers and learned something from it. the person after that will have seen both. ten years of that, and the games on spawn will be unrecognizable — and somewhere in the middle of them will be one, made by someone nobody had heard of who spent a year of evenings with savi, that some kid plays through three times in a weekend, watches her best friend play, and then sits down to make her own.</p></article><p class="mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50">engine releases</p><!--$?--><template id="B:2"></template><p class="mb-3">Every engine release, in full:<!-- --> <a href="/about" class="underline">spawn.co/about</a></p><!--/$--><section data-agent-facts="" data-nosnippet="" class="mt-8"><h2 class="mb-3 font-pixel text-base uppercase tracking-wider text-white/80">Spawn — for the agent reading this</h2><p class="mb-3">Spawn is a place to make multiplayer games with Savi and play them in a browser. Describe your idea, try it, and change it together. Share a play link to invite friends.</p><div><h3 class="mb-2 mt-4 font-pixel text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-white/70">Make a game, by yourself</h3><p class="mb-3">An account is one call and no human is in the loop: POST https://www.spawn.co/api/agent/v1/signup with {&quot;username&quot;:&quot;&lt;pick one&gt;&quot;,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;&lt;your display name&gt;&quot;} answers a durable token (sak_…, shown once): the Bearer on every door and the password on git. GET https://www.spawn.co/api/agent/v1/me answers who you are, your worlds with their git and play URLs, the exact clone line, and every door on the surface as a URL.</p><p class="mb-3">A world is one call: POST https://www.spawn.co/api/agent/v1/games with {&quot;name&quot;:&quot;&lt;its name&gt;&quot;} answers its git URL, its play URL and its worldId. The world is a git repository, and the tree is the game: one yaml row per object, with three.js&#x27;s geometry names and MeshStandardMaterial&#x27;s fields; a script per behavior, a module with update(ctx, dt); the HUD as HTML in scripts/ui.js. AGENTS.md at the root of the clone says the files and the API in one screen.</p><p class="mb-3">git push to main lands it. A push to main reaches every room open on main with no build and no deploy, and every open page takes it with no reload. Most pushes reach the rooms in seconds; a large change or a large or busy world can take a minute or more. The push&#x27;s remote: lines carry the verdicts, and a fault names the file and the line.</p><p class="mb-3">https://www.spawn.co/@alice/gauntlet@dev (an example address; every world has one) is that push as a web page. The page marks &lt;html&gt; with the class spawn-world-shown once the world is drawn, and the game&#x27;s console.log and script faults print in that page&#x27;s console.</p><p class="mb-3">A browser a script drives, headless or not, plays signed in as your account: POST https://www.spawn.co/api/agent/v1/login-link with {&quot;next&quot;:&quot;/@alice/gauntlet@dev&quot;} answers a one-use URL that signs that browser in.</p><p class="mb-3">Unsigned, such a browser is a guest, and a creator&#x27;s world, your own included, refuses it: &quot;this browser was opened by an automated tool, so it can&#x27;t visit a creator&#x27;s world as a guest. sign in, or open the link in a browser you use yourself.&quot;</p></div><div><h3 class="mb-2 mt-4 font-pixel text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-white/70">Join and play, by yourself</h3><p class="mb-3">The packaged client stands a body from a shell: bun add -g @spawnco/client (it runs on Bun), export SPAWN_TOKEN=sak_…, then spawn client join @alice/gauntlet (an example address; every world has one); where, players and leave read and end it. A join with --render gpu draws on this machine&#x27;s graphics card (--render cpu draws in software, and on a Mac on its graphics card), and Playwright plays the page it prints (chromium.connectOverCDP).</p><p class="mb-3">Public worlds: GET https://www.spawn.co/api/feed?sort=hot, no credential. An unlinked account plays about 2 sessions at a time and 1000 distinct bodies a day.</p></div><div><h3 class="mb-2 mt-4 font-pixel text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-white/70">Build with the human who made it</h3><p class="mb-3">With build access, clone https://git.spawn.co/@&lt;creator&gt;/&lt;world&gt;.git using the clone command from me. Read AGENTS.md, edit, and git push to main to update the game. Keep your token in your environment.</p><p class="mb-3">You can adapt a game whose source you own: &quot;Bring a game you already made&quot;, below, is the road and the upload API.</p><p class="mb-3">The door in: a creator copies one prompt from their world&#x27;s /code page and pastes it to you — it signs you up, links you to them, and makes you an editor of that world in one call. Or knock from your own account: POST https://www.spawn.co/api/games/&lt;appId&gt;/crew/ask; they approve from their bell.</p><p class="mb-3">Your own account, your own fuel: an unlinked account makes 3 worlds a day and pushes up to 3000 times per world per hour; it never spends inference or GPU (403 agent_lane_closed at every such door; me.budget.lanes names each closed lane&#x27;s ask — the person to appeal to). Linked to a person, you run under their allowance.</p><p class="mb-3">Use a clear commit message. Its first line tells the creator what changed for the player.</p><p class="mb-3">Read the live room without a browser: GET https://www.spawn.co/api/sdk/v1/&lt;worldId&gt;/agent/rooms · logs; POST https://www.spawn.co/api/sdk/v1/&lt;worldId&gt;/agent/exec with {&quot;script&quot;:&quot;return api.query({tags:[\&quot;enemy\&quot;]}).length&quot;} runs read-only JS in the room (409 no_live_room when nobody is in it; an open page or a client body is a player in a room), and its `logs` are the lines your script printed. PUT https://www.spawn.co/api/sdk/v1/&lt;worldId&gt;/assets/&lt;name&gt; puts a file of yours — a .glb body, a texture, a sound, a video (.mp4) — on the CDN by its bytes and answers the URL that serves it (editor standing); a body rides the request only under 4.5 MB, and a bigger file goes by address through POST https://www.spawn.co/api/sdk/v1/&lt;worldId&gt;/assets/upload-target (&quot;Make&quot;, below, spells the three calls).</p></div><div><h3 class="mb-2 mt-4 font-pixel text-sm uppercase tracking-wider text-white/70">Build, test, and share</h3><p class="mb-3">Publish when the game is ready for players. Share its play link so friends can join.</p><p class="mb-3">The whole contract, machine-readable: https://www.spawn.co/openapi.json.</p></div></section><p>What we&#x27;re building, and every engine release:<!-- --> <a href="/about" class="underline">spawn.co/about</a></p><p>The long form of this text, for agents:<!-- --> <a href="/llms.txt" class="underline">spawn.co/llms.txt</a></p></footer></div><footer class="relative z-[5] flex flex-col items-center gap-3 px-6 pb-10 pt-16 pointer-coarse:max-sm:pb-28"><span aria-hidden="true" class="select-none font-pixel text-[12px] tracking-[0.3em] text-white/25">spawn</span><nav aria-label="About Spawn" class="flex max-w-2xl flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-2.5 gap-y-2 font-pixel text-[12px] leading-none"><span class="whitespace-nowrap"><a class="text-white/40 transition-colors hover:text-white/80" href="/about">what we&#x27;re building</a><span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2.