p><p>44 updates since release, the newest 2026-11-14.</p><div><h5>Newest update<!-- -->: Rare Cards<!-- --> (2026-11-14)</h5><ul><li>Level-up cards now come in silver, gold and prismatic. Gold and prismatic are rare at first and get likelier the more runs you play. Gold and prismatic cards can deal 10 new one-of-a-kind perks: Second Wind, Hot Hands, Slam Echo, Greed Finger, Quickdraw, Ghost Hand, Midas Touch, Chain Reaction, Glass Cannon and Finger Guns Up. Close All Windows now also stops popups that were about to open.</li></ul></div><div><h5>Earlier update<!-- -->: The Slide &amp; Slam Update<!-- --> (2026-11-14)</h5><ul><li>Ground slams hit harder the higher you fall, and Spring Ring triple-jump slams send out a growing fire wave</li><li>Slide Speed level-ups leave a burning trail, stamina is gone and sprint is unlimited</li><li>Jazz Hands can make enemies dance with music, and ROCKSTAR fires black notes</li><li>New LASER LACQUER coat, laser Ricochet, Split Ring lasers and chaining beams</li><li>Wedding Ring heals co-op partners who stay close</li></ul></div><div><h5>Earlier update<!-- -->: Balance &amp; Breakables<!-- --> (2026-11-13)</h5><ul><li>YIN &amp; YANG hits way harder: freeze then burn (or burn then freeze) triggers BALANCE for 2.2x damage and a burst</li><li>MINIGUN FINGERS spin up faster, hit harder and reload quicker</li><li>Punch, slide or slam to smash loose props; floor spikes are gone</li><li>Cleaner headshots and hit markers, and fewer floating particles</li><li>Right-click the desktop to Close All Windows at once</li></ul></div><div><h5>Earlier update<!-- -->: NAIL POLISH SALOON<!-- --> (2026-11-12)</h5><ul><li>Paint every finger: nail polish coats per hand, with named pairs that combo into new shots</li><li>AKIMBO FINGUNS reload faster with a goofy full 360 twirl on both hands</li><li>Daily Run: one hand, no boxes, floors rotate each day as a surprise, hands unlock only when you beat it</li><li>Boomerang Ring flies straight and curves back gently; shots follow your crosshair</li><li>Cleaner hits: no more black scorch holes on the ground, softer nail glow</li></ul></div><div><h5>Earlier update<!-- -->: NAIL POLISH SALOON<!-- --> (2026-11-12)</h5><ul><li>Paint every finger: each hand wears its own polish coats, and every coat changes your shots</li><li>Mix two coats on one hand for named combo synergies</li><li>Daily Run is pure: one hand, no boxes, no unlocks until you beat all 5 floors</li><li>Boomerang Ring flies straight out and curves back gently, shots land on your crosshair</li><li>FINGUN buffed, softer polish glow, smaller Win98 notices</li></ul></div><div><h5>What players say</h5><ul><li><p>@flipchar · loved it · 2026-11-09 · played 13 min · 2 hearts<!-- -->: “<!-- -->Great game! However, I can&#x27;t move my cards into an empty column unless it&#x27;s a King. So I&#x27;m stuck. HELP!!!<!-- -->”</p><ul><li>@drift_knight_43<!-- --> (maker)<!-- --> replied <!-- -->2026-11-09<!-- -->: “<!-- -->Did not know someone would actually play the minigames 😂 should be fixed by now<!-- -->”</li><li>@flipchar<!-- --> replied <!-- -->2026-11-09<!-- -->: “<!-- -->@drift_knight_43 The... minigames? What do you mean? 

Anyway, I absolutely love your game here. What a great concept. I&#x27;ve played many card games in my days, but never this one. 5 STARS<!-- -->”</li><li>@poopy31016<!-- --> replied <!-- -->2026-11-10<!-- -->: “<!-- -->@flipchar he probally meant the games you play<!-- -->”</li></ul></li><li><p>@lego · loved it · 2026-11-13 · played 21 min · 1 heart<!-- -->: “<!-- -->Yeah, It&#x27;s DEBT.exe time<!-- -->”</p><ul><li>@drift_knight_43<!-- --> (maker)<!-- --> replied <!-- -->2026-11-13<!-- -->: “<!-- -->Xd ty for playing &lt;3<!-- -->”</li></ul></li><li><p>@yujiro · loved it · 2026-11-11 · played 5 min · 1 heart<!-- -->: “<!-- -->I love playing this game. Frost Hands is my favorite ability so far. Its projectiles can bounce off walls and freeze enemies, giving me more time to dodge attacks, plan my next move, or set up a strategy.<!-- -->”</p><ul><li>@drift_knight_43<!-- --> (maker)<!-- --> replied <!-- -->2026-11-11<!-- -->: “<!-- -->Thx for playing &lt;3<!-- -->”</li></ul></li><li><p>@yzykyl · loved it · 2026-11-10 · played 16 min · 1 heart<!-- -->: “<!-- -->Just floor 2 and I&#x27;m already getting destroyed😂I guess it&#x27;s time to think of a good build path for the upgrades. Love the slide movement to pair with this shooter. Incredibly action-packed. Also commend the creativity with the desktop menu and Gary!<!-- -->”</p><ul><li>@drift_knight_43<!-- --> (maker)<!-- --> replied <!-- -->2026-11-10<!-- -->: “<!-- -->&lt;3<!-- -->”</li></ul></li><li><p>@sovos · loved it · 2026-11-10 · played 3 hrs 8 min · 1 heart<!-- -->: “<!-- -->See you on the leaderboards people!<!-- -->”</p></li></ul></div></article><article><h4><a href="/@sath/rot">ROT</a></h4><p>By <a href="/@sath">@sath</a>. Published 2026-10-27<!-- -->. Last updated 2026-11-05<!-- -->.</p><p>A plague-doctor survivors game. Wikk comes home to a burned village and brews the plague that turns the kingdom&#x27;s army on itself. Stack the Dose, spread the rot, outlast the horde.</p><p>Categories: <!-- -->Survivors, Roguelite, Action<!-- -->.</p><p>Reviews: Positive · 91% loved it · 12 votes · 14 reviews and replies · 46 likes · 704 plays<!-- -->.</p><p>Released 2026-10-27. <!-- -->22 updates since release, the newest 2026-11-05.</p><div><h5>Newest update<!-- -->: Small patch: Bloodletter refined<!-- --> (2026-11-05)</h5><ul><li>Bloodletter: the bleed now cuts. Every half second it deals 1 damage to the man you cut and to anyone walking his blood trail.</li><li>Bloodletter: bleed hits never land the killing blow; they stop at 1 health. Exsanguinate&#x27;s execute is the one exception.</li><li>Bloodletter: a man who dies still bleeding keeps spurting on enemies close to his corpse until the bleed runs out.</li><li>Weapon rack: each weapon answers only inside its own slot, so a neighbour no longer steals your click.</li><li>Weapon rack: Wikk redraws faster when you pick a new weapon.</li></ul></div><div><h5>Earlier update<!-- -->: Locusts and Letters<!-- --> (2026-11-03)</h5><ul><li>Plague: The Cloud now merges touching locust swarms into one giant swarm, as big as all your swarm slots together.</li><li>Enemies: footmen are the army now. Specialists come rarer, but every one of their attacks hits harder.</li><li>Lag: locust swarms hunt and bite in turns, so big swarm fights stop hitching.</li><li>Vivarium: every post is checked whole before it goes up.</li></ul></div><div><h5>Earlier update<!-- -->: Specialize<!-- --> (2026-11-03)</h5><ul><li>WEAPON UPGRADES</li><li>Specialize (new): at the second-weapon pick (level 15, sooner with Second Arm) a SPECIALIZE card sits beside the weapons. Take it and you carry no second weapon: your first weapon&#x27;s row holds 6 different upgrades instead of 3 for the rest of the run. Why: a one-weapon build had nowhere to grow once its row was full.</li><li>Lingering Fog: lasts 1.5s a rank, 7.5s at rank V (was 0.4s to 2s), and Fog Bank is 50% wider. It doses the moment it lands and fades out instead of cutting off. Why: the cloud was fully see-through and gone too fast to matter.</li><li>Lingering Fog: each cloud drifts to the nearest enemy within 12m that no other cloud is riding, latches onto his chest and doses him every 0.5s. When he dies it hunts again. 8 clouds at most.</li><li>DOCTOR UPGRADES</li><li>Beaked Mask: the mark is now a thick blood-red crosshair pinned to the target&#x27;s head, drawn over every other effect. A sniff plays when it lands, and the bonus Ichor bursts in your plague&#x27;s colour on the kill.</li><li>PLAGUE UPGRADES</li><li>Gilded Touch: reach is +0.1m a rank (was 0.05m), so 2m at rank V. Why: the old reach was too short to notice.</li></ul></div><div><h5>Earlier update<!-- -->: Chains and Shards<!-- --> (2026-11-02)</h5><ul><li>A NOTE FROM THE DOCTOR</li><li>Sorry this update took so long to reach you. It&#x27;s a big one, and I wanted it right. If anything seems bugged or isn&#x27;t working the way it should, or if something just feels bad or off, please tell me as soon as you can, in the Vivarium or in Spawn chat. Thank you for playing.</li><li>BOSSES</li><li>The Taxman: The Collection now drags you in for 3.2s (was 1.2s) and you can&#x27;t dodge out once the chains lock. The chains then swing for the whole attack in rings that turn in opposite directions, and he walks after you while they spin. Only the swinging chains deal damage; the pull-in deals none. Why: the old pull ended before it read as a threat.</li><li>The Taxman: The Tithe, Collection and Ledger each have their own painting now, instead of one sack of coins for everything.</li><li>Captain Hollis: A Burning Furrow runs 22m (was 12m). Why: the short furrow was easy to step around.</li><li>Court Sorcerer Vex: The Star fires 5 beams (was 6). Why: six beams left no gap you could read.</li><li>The Jester: Juggle now throws gas bombs that leave a slowing cloud and mark you Giddy (damage 10 to 6). New move, Cartwheel: he tumbles straight through you. Pratfall now pays off Giddy: FLAT ON YOUR BACK roots you.</li></ul></div><div><h5>Earlier update<!-- -->: Steadier Rot<!-- --> (2026-10-31)</h5><ul><li>WEAPONS</li><li>Extra Attacks: now apply to each weapon separately instead of being shared across all of them.</li><li>Plaguethrower: a soldier caught in two or three jets of one puff now takes each jet&#x27;s full dose and burn.</li><li>Hook and Lighthouse Lantern: Twin Dose adds exactly one more hook or one more beam, instead of repeating the whole volley.</li><li>Censer: doses faster, and attack speed now raises its dose rate. Attack speed is counted once (it was being applied twice).</li><li>Censer: the aura is now two painted rings that rotate smoothly around Wikk. Fixed the rings blinking off and stuttering as they turned.</li><li>Chalk: the line now lasts 8s. Long Reach now also raises walk speed while holding Chalk.</li><li>Lighthouse Lantern: drops every 10s. Attack speed now speeds up the beam&#x27;s ticks instead of the drop rate.</li></ul></div><div><h5>What players say</h5><ul><li><p>@makeriffic · loved it · 2026-11-05 · played 20 min<!-- -->: “<!-- -->I think the game is fun and I really enjoyed it. However, the upgrade progression seems to be too slow for me. The marrows for permanent buffs are way too hard to collect. The enemies are too early too increase its number. But I still had fun! GGs<!-- -->”</p><ul><li>@sath<!-- --> (maker)<!-- --> replied <!-- -->2026-11-05<!-- -->: “<!-- -->Thanks for playing! You may not know this, but you dont just get marrow from boss kills, you can also get it from the breakables on the map and if you make it to endless each enemy has a chance of granting 1 marrow on death, which scales up to 5% per enemy chance the longer you hold out for. I will update the bone shrine so this information is more clear though and think about other ways i might make the marrow gathering more engaging.<!-- -->”</li></ul></li><li><p>@giraffe · 2026-11-03 · played 2 min<!-- -->: “<!-- -->The load screen, art work and thought put into this is excellent. 