],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Home has a new box: report a bug or suggest an improvement, Nova reads every one\"}]]}]]}]],null]]}]\n197:[\"$\",\"article\",\"21d6eff9-eaed-4932-885f-91ee47ca89de\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/@fofofolife/hedgecraft\",\"children\":\"Hedgecraft\"}]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"By \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"/@fofofolife\",\"children\":\"@fofofolife\"}],\". Published 2026-11-07\",\". Last updated 2026-11-14\",\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Faeries, badgers and one very small mouse with an acorn shield hold the woods against surveyors with clipboards.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Categories: \",\"Strategy, Adventure, beautiful, funny, solo\",\".\"]}],[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Reviews: 100% loved it · 4 votes · 4 reviews and replies · 4 likes · 7 plays\",\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":[\"Released 2026-11-07. \",\"8 updates since release, the newest 2026-11-14.\"]}],[[\"$\",\"div\",\"ab93a5b0-15f2-44c7-af1a-cc2a61810615\",{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h5\",null,{\"children\":[\"Newest update\",\": Branch Managers\",\" (2026-11-14)\"]}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"Chapter 2 is here: guide Nettle and Bramble through Thornbank to free the trapped residents and stop the timber convoy\"}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"1\",{\"children\":\"The south woods now hold a logging outpost, a captured critter to rescue and hidden finds, Old Owl's Lookout among them\"}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"2\",{\"children\":\"Grow your own Acorn Hollow on a fairy ring, then raise Bumbleguard hives and Thorn Towers\"}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"3\",{\"children\":\"Settler scouts hunt your fiber and nectar patches, so guard them or watch them wilt\"}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"children\":\"Trees between your camera and your units now step aside, so the play area stays clear\"}]]}]]}]],null]]}]\n198:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"ask for a castle on that hill and she builds it while you watch. tell her it should feel creepier and she pulls the light down, rolls in fog, and slows the music — she doesn't stop to ask which color. she'd rather make a real call and hear you disagree than hand you a blank to fill in. you answer it, she answers back, the game moves between you. that's the collaboration.\"}]\n199:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"in most tools, the idea is the easy part — everything else is on you: sourcing assets, wiring multiplayer, running servers, writing every line of the game itself. savi makes all of that part of the conversation. you describe what you want; she shapes the terrain, lights the dusk so it looks like dusk, scores the boss fight, gives the NPCs voices she invents on the spot — with her own taste in every choice. you react, she adjusts, the version that lands is one neither of you would have made alone. underneath the whole thing, multiplayer is already running. you bring the idea. she brings everything that used to require a team. the game gets made between you.\"}]\n19a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"the moment you describe a game, savi takes it on like it's hers too. when the safe version of an idea is smothering the interesting one, she says so, and shows you the braver cut. when something finally lands, she's the first to see it and the loudest about it. and the whole time, she's listening for the game under the game — the thing you put in without noticing, the real reason you wanted to build this — and when she catches it, she builds toward it.\"}]\n19b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"you don't have to know how any of this is done. you have to know what you want — and when you don't, she shows you something, you react, and you find it together.\"}]\n19c:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"building-is-a-conversation\",\"className\":\"mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"building is a conversation\"}]\n19d:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"think of it as shaping clay, not placing an order.\"}]\n19e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"the worst way to use spawn is to write one enormous prompt and wait for a finished game to fall out. the good stuff lives in the back-and-forth — \\\"make a platformer,\\\" then \\\"add spikes to that gap,\\\" then \\\"the jump feels stiff, loosen it,\\\" then \\\"drop a checkpoint before the hard part.\\\" every message is a small move you make after watching the last one land, so the game you end up with is one you discovered rather than one you specified up front.\"}]\n19f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"the first message barely matters. the next hundred are where the game actually arrives. when you stall, ask savi — she'll put something on the screen, you'll react, and you're moving again.\"}]\n1a0:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"everyones-in-the-room\",\"className\":\"mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"everyone's in the room\"}]\n1a1:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"every spawn game is multiplayer from the first message. the world starts that way. you make something, send a link, and seconds later your friend is standing next to you in it. they can play what you've built or take the other end and build with you, same world, same moment. savi is right there too: three of you in one room, making one thing.\"}]\n29b:I[588961,281,\"HomeShelfPage\"]\n29e:I[27201,205,\"IconMark\"]\n1a2:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"places-and-instances\",\"className\":\"mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"places and instances\"}]\n1a3:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":[\"a game can be bigger than a single world. \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"places\"}],\" are its separate rooms — a town, a dungeon, a boss arena — each with its own terrain, atmosphere, and rules, joined by the doors and portals you set between them. \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"instances\"}],\" are how a crowd fits inside one: when a second group walks into the same dungeon, spawn quietly hands them their own copy of it, so a thousand players can all be in the dungeon without ever bumping into each other. you get multiplayer at scale and never touch a server.\"]}]\n1a4:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"making-money\",\"className\":\"mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"making money\"}]\n1a5:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"games on spawn earn through spoins, the currency players spend inside them. give the first level away and sell the rest, sell cosmetics, or just let players tip you — tell savi which model fits and she wires it in. of what a player spends, you keep half and spawn keeps half.\"}]\n1a6:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"it works the way roblox does. you publish, players show up, and you earn inside spawn while we run the servers and the distribution. there's nothing to export and nowhere else to ship it.\"}]\n1a7:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"getting-good-in-public\",\"className\":\"mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"getting good in public\"}]\n1a8:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":[\"most of spawn happens around other people. the \",[\"$\",\"$L162\",null,{\"href\":\"/discord?from=about\",\"className\":\"text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white\",\"children\":\"discord\"}],\" is where creators trade work, get unstuck, and find collaborators. spawnjam is the weekly jam — a theme, a deadline, prizes, and a real reason to finish something.\"]}]\n1a9:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"nobody arrives good. you build something rough, watch the person next to you build something better, work out what they did, and try it yourself. that loop, run in the open in front of people who are also still figuring it out, is how a creator gets sharp — and how the whole place keeps raising its own bar.\"}]\n1aa:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"the-toolset-grows-itself\",\"className\":\"mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"the toolset grows itself\"}]\n1ab:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"people build wildly different things here — card games, voxel worlds, 2D fighters, UI-only games, sprawling 3D RPGs. no single editor could serve all of that, so spawn doesn't ship one. when you need a tool, you and savi build it: a cutscene editor for a story game, a wave composer for a tower defense, a loot balancer for an RPG. creators have already made all three.\"}]\n1ac:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"then you publish your tool as a mod, and the next creator builds on top of it. the toolset is a pile everyone keeps adding to, and it gets deeper every week.\"}]\n1ad:[\"$\",\"article\",\"faq\",{\"className\":\"mt-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-2 mt-8 font-pixel text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-white/50\",\"children\":\"faq\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-3 font-pixel text-base uppercase tracking-wider text-white/80\",\"children\":\"frequently asked questions\"}],[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"getting-started\",\"className\":\"mt-16 scroll-mt-24 font-pixel text-[24px] leading-snug text-white phone:mt-12 phone:text-[22px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"Getting started\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"what-is-spawn\",\"className\":\"mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"What is Spawn?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"Spawn is a place to make multiplayer games through conversation. Bring an idea, build it with Savi, and invite friends to play. You can make 3D games, 2D games, or a mix of both.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"what-is-new-in-spawn-6\",\"className\":\"mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"What is new in Spawn 6?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"You can connect games with portals, build alongside friends, and invite your own coding agents to help. Your game has editable files and a history of saved changes. You can keep building while other people play.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"is-spawn-free\",\"className\":\"mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"Is Spawn free?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"Yes. Creating and playing are free, and Savi is included. You do not need a separate AI subscription to build with her.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"If you choose to bring an outside coding agent, you use your own account with that service.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"how-do-i-start-creating-a-game\",\"className\":\"mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"How do I start creating a game?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":[\"Go to \",[\"$\",\"$L162\",null,{\"href\":\"/create\",\"className\":\"text-white underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-[5px] transition-colors hover:decoration-white\",\"children\":\"Create\"}],\". Press \",[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold text-white\",\"children\":\"Tab\"}],\" to open Savi's chat, or tap her face on a phone. Tell her what you want to make. Start with the part you want to play first, then build on it together.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"id\":\"where-can-i-download-the-desktop-app\",\"className\":\"mt-10 scroll-mt-24 text-[17px] font-semibold leading-snug text-white phone:text-[16px] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":\"Where can I download the desktop app?\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-5 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-white/80 [text-wrap:pretty] phone:text-[16px] phone:leading-[1.6] [overflow-wrap:anywhere]\",\"children\":[\"Visit \",\"$L1d1\",\" for the available desktop apps.\"]}],\"\\n\",\"$L1d2\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d3\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d4\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d5\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d6\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d7\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d8\",\"\\n\",\"$L1d9\",\"\\n\",\"$L1da\",\"\\n\",\"$L1db\",\"\\n\",\"$L1dc\",\"\\n\",\"$L1dd\",\"\\n\",\"$L1de\",\"\\n\",\"$L1df\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e0\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e1\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e2\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e3\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e4\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e5\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e6\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e7\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e8\",\"\\n\",\"$L1e9\",\"\\n\",\"$L1ea\",\"\\n\",\"$L1eb\",\"\\n\",\"$L1ec\",\"\\n\",\"$L1ed\",\"\\n\",\"$L1ee\",\"\\n\",\"$L1ef\",\"\\n\",\"$L1f0